        "original_id": "64dfb684-fc00-505b-baba-3f067b8cac0f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ernst John von Freyend, Wilhelm Keitel\n- Organizations: Oberkommando der Wehrmacht, Armed Forces High Command, Nazi Germany\n- Roles: adjutant, officer, field marshal, Chief of the Armed Forces High Command\n- Events: World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Wilhelm Keitel was born on 22 September 1882 and died on 16 October 1946.\n- Ernst John von Freyend was born on 25 March 1909 and died on 24 March 1980.\n- During World War II, Wilhelm Keitel was a German field marshal and served as Chief of the Armed Forces High Command, also called the Oberkommando der Wehrmacht, in Nazi Germany.\n- During World War II, Ernst John von Freyend was a German Oberkommando der Wehrmacht officer who served as adjutant to Field Marshal Wilhelm Keitel.",
